    - target: {fileID: 1736223423933981007, guid: 96048391e5bc0af49b1edfa6e3a2427c, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Velvet can be made from synthetic or natural fibers. What gives velvet
        its unique appearance is its tufting. This means that velvet fibers point
        outwards from the surface which causes surfaces directly facing the viewer
        to appear darker.
